                <pb facs="0284" n="178" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg178"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Wilson to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <hi rendition="#italic"><date
                                calendar="gregorian" when="1906-04-11">April 11,
                        1906</date></hi>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Wilson states that in the written reply which he has now received from the
                    minister for foreign affairs the verbal assurances reported in his telegram of
                    the 5th instant are confirmed and Japan’s earnest adherence to the open-door
                    policy in Manchuria emphasized.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
